<!--
  Native ClickHouse Prometheus metrics endpoint, production-only.

  Mounted at /etc/clickhouse-server/config.d/prometheus.xml by the
  production compose overlay. Not mounted in the local-development
  stack because there is no scrape target locally.

  ## Listener binding — every listen_host, not loopback

  ClickHouse binds `prometheus.port` on the top-level `listen_host`
  list, like every other port, and nothing reads a `<listen_host>`
  under `<prometheus>`. The image sets `::` and `0.0.0.0`, so the
  endpoint listens on every interface inside the container. Checked
  on ch-prod-01 on 2026-11-27: `ss` in the container's namespace
  shows `0.0.0.0:9363`, and `wget http://clickhouse:9363/metrics`
  from the Caddy container returns the metrics. An earlier version
  of this file set `<listen_host>127.0.0.1</listen_host>` here and
  said it closed the bridge; it never did.

  The endpoint accepts **no authentication of any kind**, so any
  container on the Compose network can read it. It is not
  published on the host (`docker-compose.prod.yml`). A scraper
  reaches it as `clickhouse:9363` over the Compose network
  (ADR 0062, decision 2); sharing the container's network namespace
  buys nothing and strands the scraper on every `clickhouse`
  restart.

  ## What is exposed

  All four CH metric families are turned on:
   - `metrics`: instantaneous counters / gauges
   - `events`: cumulative event counters since process start
   - `asynchronous_metrics`: periodically refreshed gauges
   - `errors`: per-error-code cumulative counters
-->
<clickhouse>
    <prometheus>
        <port>9363</port>
        <endpoint>/metrics</endpoint>

        <metrics>true</metrics>
        <events>true</events>
        <asynchronous_metrics>true</asynchronous_metrics>
        <errors>true</errors>
    </prometheus>
</clickhouse>
